      "content": "When framing your reef restoration results, focus on quantifiable metrics to demonstrate massive scale and success. Quantify the ecological improvement, such as the percentage increase in coral cover or the estimated biomass of returning fish populations. Furthermore, highlight the durability of your success by noting survival rates or anecdotal evidence of ecosystem stabilization over time. Presenting clear data transforms mere activity into undeniable, high-impact achievement for the reviewers.",
